<Layout title="Terms of Service | HangulEdu" description="Terms of Service for the Hangul Hero apps on Android and iOS and the hanguledu.com website: Premium subscriptions, rewarded ads, content and liability.">
  <article class="wrap sec wrap--medium prose legal">
    <h1 class="t-h1">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="t-meta">Last updated: October 28, 2026</p>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-h2">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p class="t-body">By downloading, installing, or using Learn Korean Alphabet: Hangul ("the App"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree to these terms, please do not use the App. These Terms apply to all users of the App, including users of the free and Premium versions. Your use of the hanguledu.com website ("the Website") is also governed by these Terms where they apply.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-h2">2. Description of Service</h2>
      <p class="t-body">Learn Korean Alphabet: Hangul (also referred to as Hangul Hero) is an educational mobile application developed by VIKTOR SOKOLIUK and distributed through Google Play and the Apple App Store. The App teaches you to read Korean: Hangul letter lessons, reading rules, practice drills and quizzes, vocabulary, and everyday phrases with audio and sound-by-sound breakdowns. Some features are available for free; others require a Premium subscription. The Website offers free learning pages about the Korean alphabet and phrases.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-h2">3. Premium Subscription</h2>
      <p class="t-body">The App offers Premium access through auto-renewable subscriptions, currently a monthly and an annual plan, that unlock additional content and features beyond the free tier. Prices may differ by platform, country, currency, promotions, introductory offers, and store configuration. The applicable purchase screen controls the plans and prices available to you.</p>
      <ul class="t-body">
        <li><strong>Billing:</strong> For iOS, payment is charged through the Apple App Store using your Apple Account. For Android, payment is charged through Google Play using your Google Play account. The applicable store processes the transaction.</li>
        <li><strong>Auto-renewal:</strong> Subscriptions automatically renew at the end of each billing period unless cancelled in accordance with the applicable store's rules before the renewal date.</li>
        <li><strong>Cancellation:</strong> You manage or cancel a subscription through the store account from which it was purchased, for example Apple Account subscription settings on iOS or Google Play → Subscriptions on Android. Cancellation generally takes effect at the end of the current billing period, subject to the applicable store's rules.</li>
        <li><strong>Free trials and introductory offers:</strong> An eligible plan may include a free trial or other introductory offer. Eligibility and duration are shown by the applicable store and purchase screen. Unless cancelled in accordance with the applicable store's rules, an eligible trial converts to the displayed paid subscription at the end of the trial.</li>
        <li><strong>Restore Purchases:</strong> The App provides a restore-purchases function for eligible purchases where supported by the applicable store. Restoration is subject to the store's account, transaction, and platform rules.</li>
        <li><strong>Refunds:</strong> Store purchases are processed by Apple or Google Play. Refund requests are handled under the applicable store's policies and procedures. We do not directly process refunds for purchases made through Apple or Google Play.</li>
        <li><strong>Price changes:</strong> Subscription prices and available plans may change. Any applicable notice or consent process is handled according to the applicable store's rules.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="t-body">Subscriptions are managed with RevenueCat, a third-party subscription-management service, as described in our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-h2">4. Free vs Premium</h2>
      <p class="t-body">The free version of the App includes the basic alphabet, introductory lessons, and a limited selection of phrases, with daily limits on certain activities and optional rewarded ads. Premium subscribers receive the full alphabet and learning path, all phrase packs, unlimited practice and saved words, and any future content added to the App, without daily limits and without ads. Features available in each tier are subject to change.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-h2">5. Rewarded Ads and In-App Rewards</h2>
      <p class="t-body">The free version of the App lets you watch rewarded ads to receive in-app rewards, such as an extra practice session or extra letter views.</p>
      <ul class="t-body">
        <li><strong>Optional:</strong> Watching ads is always optional. The App shows no banner or interstitial ads.</li>
        <li><strong>Rewards:</strong> A reward is granted only after the ad has been completed.</li>
        <li><strong>Limits and availability:</strong> Daily limits apply to rewarded extras, and ad availability is not guaranteed.</li>
        <li><strong>Virtual items:</strong> Rewards, XP, streaks, and badges are virtual, have no monetary value, and cannot be purchased, sold, exchanged, transferred, or redeemed for money or anything else. They may be changed or reset, including daily.</li>
        <li><strong>Premium:</strong> Premium subscribers are not shown ads.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-h2">6. Audio and Learning Content</h2>
      <p class="t-body">Korean pronunciation audio for letters and phrases is synthesized speech generated with Google Cloud Text-to-Speech, not recordings of a native speaker. Pronunciations, romanizations, translations, and usage notes are provided for learning purposes only and may contain errors or simplifications; we do not guarantee their accuracy or completeness.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
